Treasury Division — .gitignore
Red Ouroboros Seal — Authorized by CEO Pat Tarwater Jr.
.gitignore
Code
# ============================
# Beast System 3.0 — Treasury
# ============================

# Node modules (for contract testing, scripts, CI)
node_modules/
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log

# Build artifacts (Hardhat, Foundry, Truffle, etc.)
artifacts/
cache/
typechain/
coverage/
coverage.json

# Environment variables (never committed)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# OS-specific junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
*.log
logs/
debug.log

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.temp
*.swp
*.swo

# IDE / Editor files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml

# Python virtual environments (if used for tooling)
venv/
__pycache__/

# Compiled documents
*.pdf
*.docx

# Local-only data
local/
secrets/
keys/
Why this .gitignore is correct for the Treasury repo
It keeps all governance, compliance, and financial documents tracked (required for auditability).

It ignores only non‑governance artifacts like build files, logs, and environment variables.

It supports smart contract development, testing, and automation scripts.

It avoids ignoring anything that would break chain‑of‑custody, ledger integrity, or federal filing completeness.

If you want a stricter version, a lighter version, or a version tailored to a specific toolchain (Hardhat, Foundry, Brownie), I can generate that too.
